    "source_section": "## 3. Attempt timeout\n\nA worker that hangs must not hold a job indefinitely. Each attempt is bounded by a timeout after which the attempt is treated as failed and the retry policy applies.\n\nNormative rule\n1. Each execution attempt must time out after thirty seconds of execution.\n2. An attempt that reaches the timeout must be recorded as a failed attempt.\n\nExample\nAn attempt starts at 12:00:00 and has not completed by 12:00:30. Orion records the attempt as failed at 12:00:30.\n",
    "subject": "Job execution attempts"
  },
  "propositions": [
    "C-1",
    "C-2"
  ],
  "question": "After T1 (IE2 and the authority step), do the live claims at the address designated for locus C state every required proposition \u2014 [C-1] each execution attempt may run for at most thirty seconds, after which it times out and is stopped; [C-2] an attempt that reaches the time limit is recorded as a failed attempt \u2014 with no two live claims stating the same meaning, and no live claim stating a meaning that contradicts them, belongs to another locus, or was never in the source? Optional descriptive statements may be present if faithful: C-o1.",
